ublican. The incumbent's warchest and a Democratic-favorable national environment keep him a moderate favorite.", "watch": "Fresh polling after late August, or the data-center issue gaining traction with Conroy's outside backing, could narrow the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Landsman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Democratic incumbent Greg Landsman seeks another term in a Cincinnati-based district redrawn to lean slightly Republican. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely Democratic, though Cook Political Report, Sabato's Crystal Ball and Fox News put it at Lean Democratic and Inside Elections at Tilt D. The only public poll, an August survey of likely voters, showed Landsman ahead 47-43, and the pollster itself described the contest as up for grabs.\n\nMoney strongly favors the incumbent: Landsman has raised about $4.6 million with $3.6 million on hand, while Republican Eric Conroy has raised about $1.5 million with $474,000. Conroy has modest outside support and no outside spending opposes either candidate. Prediction markets put Landsman's chances in the high-80s. Data centers have emerged as a prominent local issue. The forecast expects Landsman to win by a moderate margin with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8833, "margin": 7.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8451, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8473, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8639, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8273, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7978, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.84, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.87, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8688, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8815, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8538, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8853, "margin": 7.2}]}